* E-14: the 2nd projection's template.
*
* This is the tiny metacoded-language interpreter of `metasystem-unroll.ref`,
* with its object program replaced by the token MARKER. `DsSpecialise` in
* `examples/compiler.ref` lexes this template and the program, splices the
* program's tokens in place of MARKER, and drives the result -- so the object
* program travels through the *source* rather than through the driver, and
* nothing on the driver's own chain is touched.
*
* `refal run examples/compiler.ref SPECIALISE "<this file>" "(Times ...)"`
* therefore emits the target program for the program given, which is the 2nd
* projection: the residue emits code.
*
* Object language (Turchin 1980 1.3):
*   (End)                 contribute nothing more
*   (In)                  contribute the rest of the input
*   (Lit c (P))           contribute the symbol c, then run P
*   (Seq (P) (Q))         run P, then run Q
*   (Times (Count) (P))   run P once for each mark in Count

$ENTRY Go {
  e.In = <Run MARKER e.In>;
}

Run {
  (End) e.In = ;
  (In) e.In = e.In;
  (Lit s.C t.P) e.In = s.C <Run t.P e.In>;
  (Seq t.P t.Q) e.In = <Run t.P e.In> <Run t.Q e.In>;
  (Times t.Count t.P) e.In = <Times t.Count t.P e.In>;
}

Times {
  () t.P e.In = ;
  ('*' e.Rest) t.P e.In = <Run t.P e.In> <Times (e.Rest) t.P e.In>;
}
